#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Write the branch's decision page: one local HTML page, built from the spec, the agent's decision notes, the reports,
the evidence and the pull request's CI, for one question: is this PR safe to merge, or is something missing that could
compromise system stability or the user's experience? It opens as a control panel: a verdict that comes only from
recorded values (Not ready, Your call or Ready), then one sentence each on the problem, stability, the user's experience,
testing, code review, what isn't proven, undo and your decisions. Six sections follow in order (the problem, the solution,
testing, code review, not proven, your decisions), each a native disclosure, open, with long lists folded behind their
count; then a footer with merge and ship, the reports as annexes, the pull request's quality signals from quality.jsonl
and its identifiers. Tests are grouped by layer, and those the agent ran for real show their evidence inline even when
the page showed it earlier. Figures the notes name are embedded in place, and an SVG is only ever an image. An animated
figure is a scene file: its allowlisted shapes, text and timing are validated and compiled here into inline SVG and CSS,
with no-script controls, and a refused one costs only that figure. References
link: the PR, its commits and file:line to GitHub, https URLs, and local reports and evidence by file://. A branch that
answers a question instead of shipping a change gets the investigation page, below.

When the decision notes hold a `Mode: investigation` line outside fenced blocks, it writes the investigation page
instead, for a branch that answers a question rather than ships a change: the question, the answer and its
confidence, your decisions and the blockers come first, then folded hypotheses (each with what speaks for and against
it), options, what was not checked, the findings (Supports, Refutes, Inconclusive, NOT RUN; PASS and FAIL read as
expected or not) and the reports, then a footer of identifiers. The files the notes name are embedded under the part
that names them, within the same limits. The PR, CI, verify, the stamps, the checks guide and the ship steps do not
apply to it, and it never calls gh.

  decision-report <page> <evidence dir>    run by `reports html`, which passes both paths; prints the page's path

The page runs no script and loads nothing from the network. Of the files the reports name, it reads only those inside
the evidence directory, and embeds text up to 200 KB (head and tail kept), images up to 2 MB, 20 MB in all; the rest is linked by file:// path.
Besides the reports, the change page reads the repository's ship.md under ~/.agents/repos and the review's lenses.md, bounded as a report is,
and the last 2 MB of the kit's logs/quality.jsonl for the signals `quality-log pr` recorded for the PR.
It is written to a temporary file and renamed into place; when generation fails, the page is removed and the error
printed (exit 1), so an older page is never taken for the current one.
"""
